Lower the conversion recursion cap on wasm32 (and in --cfg fuzzing builds)

CONV_DEPTH (8192) caps the nesting of whnf / is_def_eq / infer_type and
turns deeper recursion into a decline; it is sized for an 8 MB C stack.
On wasm32 guest calls run on the engine's native stack with larger
frames (wasmfuzz: 8 MiB for run-input, 32 MiB per fuzzing worker), and
the arena's perf/unfold-before-literal-bad overflowed it at 8192. The
cap is 4096 there; native builds without --cfg fuzzing keep 8192.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR; open issues #3 and #5 are
soundness reports, checked 2026-11-22).

diff --git a/src/tc.rs b/src/tc.rs
index 4b32139..219a5a2 100644
--- a/src/tc.rs
+++ b/src/tc.rs
@@ -158,7 +158,12 @@ const MAX_FALLBACK_TRIES: u32 = 4;
 /// Lean has no 2048 cap; `WellFounded.Nat.fix` / UTF-8 decode proofs nest
 /// `Nat.rec` conversion past that (Init `utf8DecodeChar?.assemble₃._proof_3`).
 /// Kept well under typical C-stack (~8MB) so this is a decline, not a segfault.
+#[cfg(not(any(target_family = "wasm", fuzzing)))]
 const CONV_DEPTH: u32 = 8_192;
+/// wasm32 guest calls run on the engine's native stack, where these frames are
+/// larger (wasmfuzz: 8 MiB for run-input, 32 MiB per fuzzing worker).
+#[cfg(any(target_family = "wasm", fuzzing))]
+const CONV_DEPTH: u32 = 4_096;
 
